{"step_index":9771,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T13:04:17Z","thinking":"The provided DOM snippet is incomplete; it cuts off mid-base64-encoded image data within the `src` attribute. This likely explains the user's difficulty and request for the complete DOM of the text box. The user's concern about the inactive button suggests a functional difference related to this incomplete data, which requires comparing the DOMs.\n\n\nThe agent already has the Run button's DOM from previous investigations. It confirmed the button's active state from the screenshot by examining its text content and visual appearance, noting the completed image token calculation. This confirms the button should be enabled, therefore DOM comparison is unneccessary.\n\n\nThe application's rapid sequence of actions caused the issue; immediate prompt injection and keyboard input triggered before image processing completed. The platform's interface disables submission during tokenization, so the keyboard shortcut was ignored. Consequently, the application entered a waiting loop as generation did not start, timing out after 45 seconds.\n\n\nThe user's observation about the Run button activation timing is likely correct. The platform likely delays enabling the Run button until token calculation completes. The goal is to implement a mechanism to detect and trigger the Run button immediately upon its activation.\n\nThe platform employs specific visual cues to signal the Run button's ready state, including text content updates, attribute changes, and the presence or absence of visual indicators. A hook can be placed to monitor these signals and trigger the button's action when the conditions for readiness are met.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Inspect Run button states during upload","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import asyncio\nimport os\nimport json\nfrom playwright.async_api import async_playwright\n\nCHROME_PROFILE = r\"D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio-vision\\chrome_profile\"\nTEST_IMAGE = r\"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\test_page1_scale2.5.webp\"\n\nasync def main():\n    async with async_playwright() as p:\n        args = [\"--disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled\", \"--start-maximized\"]\n        context = await p.chromium.launch_persistent_context(\n            user_data_dir=CHROME_PROFILE,\n            headless=False,\n            no_viewport=True,\n            args=args,\n            ignore_default_args=[\"--enable-automation\"]\n        )\n        page = context.pages[0] if context.pages else await context.new_page()\n        print(\"Navigating to AI Studio...\")\n        await page.goto(\"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat\", wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=60000)\n        await asyncio.sleep(3)\n        \n        # State 1: Empty prompt box\n        s1 = await page.evaluate('''() => {\n            const btn = document.querySelector('button.ctrl-enter, button:has(.ctrl-enter), [mattooltipclass=\"run-button-tooltip\"]');\n            if (!btn) {\n                // Search by text\n                const all = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button'));\n                const b = all.find(el => (el.innerText || '').includes('Run'));\n                if (b) {\n                    return {\n                        tag: b.tagName,\n                        outer: b.outerHTML.slice(0, 200),\n                        disabled: b.disabled,\n                        ariaDisabled: b.getAttribute('aria-disabled'),\n                        classes: b.className\n                    };\n                }\n                return null;\n            }\n            return {\n                tag: btn.tagName,\n                outer: btn.outerHTML.slice(0, 200),\n                disabled: btn.disabled,\n                ariaDisabled: btn.getAttribute('aria-disabled'),\n                classes: btn.className\n            };\n        }''')\n        print(\"State 1 (Empty):\", s1)\n        \n        # Upload image\n        file_input = page.locator('input[type=\"file\"], [data-test-upload-file-input]').first\n        await file_input.set_input_files(TEST_IMAGE)\n        print(\"Image uploaded! Monitoring Run button state every 0.5s for 10s...\")\n        \n        for i in range(20):\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.5)\n            state = await page.evaluate('''() => {\n                const all = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button'));\n                const b = all.find(el => (el.innerText || '').includes('Run') || (el.className || '').includes('ctrl-enter'));\n                if (!b) return { error: \"no button\" };\n                return {\n                    disabled: b.disabled,\n                    ariaDisabled: b.getAttribute('aria-disabled'),\n                    classes: b.className,\n                    text: (b.innerText || '').replace(/\\\\n/g, ' '),\n                    hasTokens: Boolean(document.querySelector('.media-chunk, ms-prompt-image, .loaded-image'))\n                };\n            }''')\n            print(f\"t={i*0.5:.1f}s: {state}\")\n            # If enabled, break\n            if state.get('disabled') is False and state.get('ariaDisabled') != 'true':\n                print(f\"[+] Run button is ACTIVE at t={i*0.5:.1f}s!\")\n                break\n                \n        await context.close()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(main())\n","Description":"Inspect Run button states","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\inspect_run_button_states.py","toolAction":"Writing file","toolSummary":"Write inspect_run_button_states script"}}]}
